# Feature Component Rules — Angular 21

Follow all rules in `AGENTS.md`. Additional scoped rules for feature components:

## Standalone & Signals-First (v21 defaults)
- Standalone is the default — never set `standalone: false`
- Smart components: inject services with `inject()`, manage state via signals, pass data to children via `input()`
- Presentational components: only `input()`, `output()`, `model()` — no service injection
- Use `linkedSignal()` to derive an editable signal from another signal
- Use `resource()` / `httpResource()` for data loading instead of manual subscribe
- Use `@let` for template-local derived values (instead of pipes/methods)
- Use signal queries (`viewChild()`, `contentChild()`, etc.) instead of decorators

## Templates
- `@for` with `track` expression (not `*ngFor` / `trackBy`)
- `@if` / `@else if` / `@else` for conditionals (not `*ngIf`)
- `@switch` / `@case` / `@default` for branching
- `@defer (on viewport | idle | interaction)` for non-critical UI
- `[class.x]` / `[style.y]` over `ngClass` / `ngStyle`
- Selectorless components (experimental in v21): opt-in only, greenfield code

## File Structure
- New convention: `{feature}-{name}.ts` exporting `class FeatureName` with `app-feature-name` selector
- Legacy convention: `{feature}-{name}.component.ts` — keep when matching existing files
- Separate `.html` and `.scss`/`.css` files
- `OnPush` change detection always
- Cleanup subscriptions with `takeUntilDestroyed()` or `DestroyRef`

## Anti-patterns
- No business logic in presentational components
- No manual HTTP subscribe when `httpResource()` fits
- No `@Input()` / `@Output()` decorators (use signal APIs)
- No `@ViewChild` / `@ContentChild` decorators (use signal queries)
- No `*ngIf` / `*ngFor` / `*ngSwitch` (deprecated in v21)
- No `ngClass` / `ngStyle` (soft-deprecated in v21)
